[IQ Generator Preset]
# Lesson 11: binary FSK.
# Each bit selects one of two tones, 500 Hz either side of the carrier here (tone spacing 1000 Hz, symbol rate 1000 Bd, so the modulation index h = 1). Open the Frequency tab and zoom in on the first few symbols: the orange line is the tone of each symbol and the blue line is the frequency measured from the phase step between samples. Before noise the envelope never changes (PAPR 0 dB), which is why FSK suits efficient nonlinear amplifiers. On the Spectrum tab look for two lobes at the tone frequencies. Try raising the SNR or changing the tone spacing.
Version=4
Modulation=2-FSK
NumberOfSymbols=256
SymbolRateBaud=1000
SamplesPerSymbol=8
Pulse=RRC
RRCBeta=0.2
SpanSymbols=10
AmplitudeGain=1
